      "text": "709340968.\n```<\uff5cUser\uff5c>\nPlease solve the math problem.\nQuestion: What is the sum of 833931691 and 579314615? Please reason step by step.\n<\uff5cAssistant\uff5c>\nTo find the sum of 833931691 and 579314615, we can follow these steps:\n\n1. Write down the numbers one below the other, aligning them by their place values (ones, tens, hundreds, etc.).\n2. Add the digits in the ones place: 1 + 5 = 6.\n3. Add the digits in the tens place: 9 + 1 = 10. Write down 0 and carry over 1 to the hundreds place.\n4. Add the digits in the hundreds place, including the carry-over: 6 + 4 + 1 = 11. Write down 1 and carry over 1 to the thousands place.\n5. Add the digits in the thousands place, including the carry-over: 1 + 3 + 9 + 1 = 14. Write down 4 and carry over 1 to the ten-thousands place.\n6. Add the digits in the ten-thousands place, including the carry-over: 1 + 3 + 9 + 1 = 14. Write down 4 and carry over 1 to the hundred-thousands place.\n7. Add the digits in the hundred-thousands place, including the carry-over: 1 + 3 + 9 + 1 = 14. Write down 4 and carry over 1 to the million place.\n8. Add the digits in the million place, including the carry-over: 1 + 3 + 9 + 1 = 14. Write down 4 and carry over 1 to the ten-million place.\n9. Add the digits in the ten-million place, including the carry-over: 1 + 3 + 9 + 1 = 14. Write down 4 and carry over 1 to the hundred-million place.\n10. Add the digits in the hundred-million place, including the carry-over: 1 + 3 + 9 + 1 = 14. Write down 4 and carry over 1 to the billion place.\n11. Add the digits in the billion place, including the carry-over: 1 + 3 + 9 + 1 = 14. Write down 4 and carry over 1 to the trillion place.\n\nNow, let's put it all together:\n\n```\n  833931691\n+ 579314615\n--------\n  1413246306\n```\n\nTherefore, the sum of 833931691 and 579314615 is 1413246306.\n</think>\n<answer>\n1413246306\n</answer>",
